# Deployment Integration Rules (MANDATORY)

**Status**: MANDATORY
**Effective**: 2025-10-27 (Post Epic 006 - 100% CI/CD Automation)
**Applies To**: ALL code changes

## Overview

Following Epic 006 completion, Sovren has **100% CI/CD automation** with zero-downtime blue-green deployments. **ALL code changes MUST integrate with automated pipelines.**

## Mandatory Requirements

### 1. Story Completion Criteria

Stories are **NOT COMPLETE** until:
- ✅ CI/CD quality gates passing
- ✅ Staging deployment successful
- ✅ Health checks passing (/health, /ready, /live, /detailed)
- ✅ Smoke tests passing (28/28 tests)
- ✅ Deployment status documented in completion summary

### 2. Health Check Endpoints

**All new backend services MUST implement**:

```typescript
// packages/backend/src/routes/health.ts

app.get('/health', (req, res) => {
  res.json({
    status: 'healthy',
    service: 'service-name',
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    uptime: process.uptime(),
    version: process.env.APP_VERSION
  });
});

app.get('/ready', async (req, res) => {
  const dbHealthy = await checkDatabaseConnection();
  const cacheHealthy = await checkCacheConnection();

  if (dbHealthy && cacheHealthy) {
    res.json({ status: 'ready' });
  } else {
    res.status(503).json({ status: 'not ready' });
  }
});

app.get('/live', (req, res) => {
  res.json({ status: 'alive' });
});

app.get('/detailed', async (req, res) => {
  // Admin-only detailed health report
  res.json({
    status: 'healthy',
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    services: {
      database: await getDatabaseHealth(),
      cache: await getCacheHealth(),
      external: await getExternalServicesHealth()
    },
    metrics: {
      memory: process.memoryUsage(),
      cpu: process.cpuUsage()
    }
  });
});
```

### 3. Pull Request Template

**All PRs MUST include deployment checklist**:

```markdown
## Deployment Checklist
- [ ] CI/CD checks passing
- [ ] Tests passing (≥95% coverage for services)
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] CHANGELOG.md updated
- [ ] Health check endpoints implemented (if new service)
- [ ] Ready for staging deployment

## Deployment Status (Post-Merge)
- [ ] Staging deployment: Success
- [ ] Health checks: All passing
- [ ] Smoke tests: 28/28 passing
- [ ] Production: Pending manual approval
```

### 4. Deployment Workflow

**Automatic Staging Deployment** (on merge to main):
```bash
# Triggered automatically
git push origin main

# Monitor deployment
gh run watch

# Verify staging
curl https://api-staging.sovren.dev/health
```

**Production Deployment** (manual approval):
```bash
# Trigger production deployment
gh workflow run backend-deployment.yml -f environment=production

# Approve in GitHub UI
# Actions → Backend Deployment → Review deployments → Approve

# Verify production
curl https://api.sovren.dev/health
```

### 5. Quality Gates

**Pre-Deployment** (automatic):
- ESLint: 0 errors/warnings
- TypeScript: Type checks passing
- Tests: ≥95% coverage for services
- Security: 0 high/critical vulnerabilities
- Docker: Image size < 150MB
- Trivy: Security scan clean

**Post-Deployment** (automatic):
- Deployment time: < 10 minutes
- Health checks: All passing
- Smoke tests: 28/28 passing
- Error rate: < 5%
- Response time P95: < 1000ms

### 6. Rollback Procedure

**Automatic Rollback Triggers**:
- HTTP 5xx error rate > 5% for 2 minutes
- Response time P95 > 1000ms
- Health check failures > 3 consecutive

**Manual Rollback**:
```bash
# Emergency rollback (< 2 minutes)
gh workflow run automated-rollback.yml -f environment=staging

# Or for production
gh workflow run automated-rollback.yml -f environment=production
```

## Code Patterns

### Backend Service Template

```typescript
// packages/backend/src/services/myService.ts

export class MyService {
  async initialize() {
    // Service initialization
  }

  async healthCheck(): Promise<boolean> {
    // Service-specific health check
    return true;
  }
}
```

### Frontend Component Template

```typescript
// packages/frontend/src/features/my-feature/components/MyComponent.tsx

export const MyComponent: React.FC = () => {
  // Component implementation
  return <div>My Component</div>;
};

// Required: Storybook story
// packages/frontend/src/stories/MyComponent.stories.tsx

// Required: Tests (≥80% coverage)
// packages/frontend/src/features/my-feature/__tests__/MyComponent.test.tsx
```

## Enforcement

**Automated via CI/CD**:
- Pre-commit hooks (lint, format, test)
- GitHub Actions (quality gates)
- Deployment pipeline (health checks, smoke tests)

**Manual via Code Review**:
- Deployment checklist verified
- Health check endpoints reviewed
- Documentation reviewed

